caption: Demonic Minions

Demonic Minions (Ally Group): Demon Lords can invest points into ally groups; that is, arguably, the primary thing that makes them Demon Lords. In order to create direct minions, the Demon Lord must have the souls available and must have created a template for them. Like the rules-as-written allies, the racial template for demons must be based on a percentage of the starting point value of the game, not the demon lord’s actual point value (for the Isekai game, we are calling this 200 character points). More potent racial templates can be purchased using the optional rules for “nonsentient” allies, with every 50% of the starting value adding 5 points to the base cost of the ally group. The racial template can include mundane traits and any demonic traits the GM has approved for demon lords and their minions. This can include an intuitive, racial knowledge of Sorcery, so long as the Demon Lord himself knows the spell. Demon Lords often release the tormented souls from their torment coins who have been on “good behavior” to become their demonic minions. All demonic minions count as priests to their Demon Lord, and everyone killed by a demon minion has their soul stolen and sent to that Demon Lord (assuming he has room in a torment chamber or his personal holding cells).
